Short:        Library and tool for the Divoom Pixoo 64
Author:       André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Uploader:     André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library), picture.datatype V43+
Distribution: Aminet

pixoo.library controls a Divoom Pixoo 64 LED display (also Pixoo 16/32)
over the network, through the device's small HTTP interface. PixooCtl
brings all of it to the Shell: pictures, animations, text, a clock and
slideshows on the Pixoo, straight from your Amiga.

Features
--------
 - display on/off, brightness, channel, clock face, device settings
 - 64x64 framebuffer with pixels, lines, rectangles and text, sent to
   the display with one call
 - built-in pixel font, and any Amiga bitmap font (topaz, SevenAlone ...)
 - scrolling text rendered by the device itself
 - pictures in every format the datatypes system reads (IFF, PNG, JPEG,
   ...), shrunk to fit with their aspect ratio kept; alpha channels and
   transparent colours are blended over the background
 - GIF animations (decoded by the library, up to 59 frames), played by
   the device on its own
 - PixooCtl: slideshow of a drawer, sorted or in random order
 - any TCP/IP stack with bsdsocket.library (Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami);
   plain HTTP, no SSL library needed
 - 68000 or better; network calls can be stopped with Ctrl-C

The Pixoo's interface is not officially documented; this project is not
affiliated with Divoom. Tested with a Pixoo 64 on AmigaOS 3.2.

Installation
------------
Double click Install. It copies pixoo.library to LIBS: and, if you like,
PixooCtl to C: and the developer files (headers and AmigaGuide reference)
to a drawer of your choice. PixooCtl also runs straight from the archive.

Pictures other than GIF need picture.datatype V43 or newer (AmigaOS 3.5
and later); everything else works on AmigaOS 3.0.

PixooCtl
--------
PixooCtl HOST/A,PORT/K/N,TIMEOUT/K/N,SIZE/K/N,ON/S,OFF/S,BRIGHTNESS=BRI/K/N,
 CHANNEL/K/N,CLOCK/K/N,FONT/K,FILL/K,TEST/S,CHARSET/S,TEXT/K,X/K/N,Y/K/N,
 COLOR/K,TIME/S,CLEARTEXT/S,SCROLL/K,TEXTID/K/N,DEVFONT/K/N,WIDTH/K/N,
 SPEED/K/N,DIR/K,ALIGN/K,DEMO/K/N,CMD/K,GET/K,INFO/S,IMAGE/K,ANIM/K,
 ENLARGE/S,DELAY/K/N,FRAMES/K/N,SHOW/K,PATTERN/K,SECONDS/K/N,REPEAT/S,
 RANDOM/S

 HOST              IP address or name of the Pixoo
 ON, OFF           switch the display on or off
 BRIGHTNESS=n      brightness 0-100
 CHANNEL=n         0 clock faces, 1 cloud, 2 visualizer, 3 custom
 CLOCK=n           clock face id
 FILL=RRGGBB       fill the display with one colour
 TEST              test pattern
 FONT=name/size    Amiga font for TEXT, TIME and CHARSET, e.g. topaz/8
 CHARSET           all characters of the current font
 IMAGE=file        draw a picture, shrunk to fit the display
 ANIM=file         play a GIF animation over what was drawn before
 ENLARGE           also scale small pictures up to the display size
 DELAY=n           milliseconds per frame of ANIM (default: from the file)
 FRAMES=n          most frames of ANIM, 1-59 (longer ones are thinned out)
 TEXT=text         draw text at X,Y in COLOR; "*n" starts a new line
 TIME              the current time (HH:MM), centred, in COLOR
 SCROLL=text       scrolling text drawn by the device at X,Y in COLOR,
                   over the picture shown last
 TEXTID=n          slot of the scrolling text, 0-19; another id adds a text
 DEVFONT=n         font of the device for SCROLL, 0-7
 WIDTH=n           width of the scrolling area, 16-64
 SPEED=n           milliseconds per scroll step, 0-100 (smaller is faster)
 DIR=LEFT|RIGHT    scroll direction (ignored by the firmware tested)
 ALIGN=LEFT|CENTER|RIGHT  alignment within the text area
 CLEARTEXT         remove the scrolling texts
 X=n, Y=n          position for TEXT and SCROLL
 COLOR=RRGGBB      colour for TEXT, TIME and SCROLL (default FFFFFF)
 SHOW=drawer       slideshow of the pictures in a drawer, sorted by name
 PATTERN=pattern   files for SHOW, e.g. #?.(iff|png); icons are skipped
 SECONDS=n         display time per picture of SHOW (default 10)
 REPEAT            start SHOW again after the last picture
 RANDOM            random order, new for every round
 DEMO=n            bouncing square for n frames, prints frames per second
 CMD=json          send a raw JSON command and print the answer
 GET=key           print one setting, e.g. GET=Brightness
 INFO              print all settings
 PORT, TIMEOUT, SIZE  port (80), timeout in s (5), display size (64)

FILL, TEST, CHARSET, IMAGE, TEXT and TIME draw on top of each other; the
result is sent once (or is the background of ANIM and SHOW). Ctrl-C stops
a slideshow at any time.

Examples:
 PixooCtl 192.168.1.50 IMAGE=Work:Pictures/Boing.iff TEXT="Boing!"
 PixooCtl 192.168.1.50 FONT=topaz/8 FILL=000000 TIME COLOR=00FF00
 PixooCtl 192.168.1.50 FILL=000000 ANIM=cat.gif FRAMES=20
 PixooCtl 192.168.1.50 SHOW=Work:Pictures PATTERN=#?.iff RANDOM REPEAT

Demo
----
The drawer Demo holds a Shell script that shows the main features one
after the other, with pictures drawn for it (a bouncing ball, copper bars,
a floppy disk):

 CD Demo
 Execute PixooDemo 192.168.1.50

Developers
----------
The reference of all functions, tags and error codes is
Developer/pixoo.library.guide (AmigaGuide, made from the comments of the
headers). Developer/include holds the libraries, clib, proto and inline
headers, Developer/fd and Developer/sfd the interface files. Programs open
the library like any other and then work with a handle:

 px = PixooOpen("192.168.1.50", TAG_DONE);
 PixooLoadImage(px, "Work:Pictures/Boing.iff", TAG_DONE);
 PixooPush(px);
 PixooClose(px);

The sources are in the drawer Source; they build with bebbo's amiga-gcc
cross compiler ("make"), see Source/README.md.

Contents
--------
 Install              Installer script (English/German)
 Libs/pixoo.library   the library
 PixooCtl             the Shell tool
 Demo/                demo script and pictures
 Developer/           headers, fd, sfd and AmigaGuide reference
 Source/              sources (MIT License)
 LICENSE              MIT License

